data.content:
## Breaking Changes: Microsoft.OpenApi v1 → v2 (used by .NET 10)

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgrades the underlying library from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1** to **v2**, which targets **OpenAPI 3.1**. Here are the key issues in your code:

---

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed

The `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone. `Schema.Example` is now a `JsonNode`.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (.NET 10)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

---

### 2. `OpenApiReference` / `ReferenceType` replaced with typed references

Reference wrappers are now generic. Use `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference` directly:

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After (.NET 10)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};
```

---

### 3. `schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's `type` array instead of a separate `nullable` flag. To make a property **not** nullable, ensure `"null"` is not in its type set:

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (.NET 10)
// Nullable is expressed via the Type flags enum.
// Remove the "null" type if present:
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

If you wanted to *set* nullable: `property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;`

---

### 4. `operation.Responses.TryAdd` — minor change

`OpenApiResponses` is now a plain `Dictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>`, so `TryAdd` still works. No change needed here, but note `OpenApiResponse.Description` is still required — your existing code is fine.

---

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of namespace changes:**
| Removed | Replacement |
|---------|-------------|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `JsonValue.Create(...)` |
| `OpenApiReference` + `ReferenceType` | `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("id")` |
| `schema.Nullable` | `schema.Type` flag with `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
